      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A workaround​ would be to make sure that the trigger volume that you need to enter is below the point that someone teleports to or spawns at. That way they \"fall\" a small distance to hit the trigger.\n\nNot practical in all situations, or maybe at all. But it might be a workaround you can do for now.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-05-26T15:21:55.051Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm pretty sure this is a bug, unless I'm missing something important.\n\nI have two areas in my world using two different post-processing volumes. The settings for exposure and bloom are very different.\n\nIf I am in one area, and use TeleportPlayer to go to the other area, there is a 3-4 second delay in switching between post-processing profiles, causing the player to be blinded for those seconds due to the bloom threshold being much higher in that area and having more \"normal\" exposure settings.\n\nHowever, as a test I made a new area with two cubes/colliders, using the same profiles. If I *walk* into those areas, then the switch is immediate. No blindness or anything, it's an immediate switch. \n\nI also tried making one profile global, and having the other profile within that with a different priority, just in case it was something to do with that.  Nope, the same bug occurs.\n\nIt only seems to occur when using TeleportPlayer.\n\nWould love this to be fixed, or advice if I am doing something wrong. Thanks!",
